    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`, and `pytest -q` passes (1 test). That test only checks that `LABELS` is lower-case, though. Nothing calls `label_ticket` itself, and I didn't make a live API request, so the function is untested.\n\n**What it does:** it makes one `client.messages.create` call to `MODEL` (`claude-sonnet-4-6`) with `max_tokens=5`. The system prompt tells the model to answer with exactly one word from `bug, feature, question`, and the ticket text is the user message. It joins the text in the reply, strips it and lower-cases it. If the result isn't in `LABELS`, it returns `\"question\"`.\n\n**Temperature is set differently than you'd expect.** The pinned SDK, `anthropic==1.8.0`, no longer accepts `temperature=` as an argument to `messages.create`, so passing it would raise a `TypeError`. The SDK's migration guide says to send it through `extra_body` instead, so every request includes `extra_body={\"temperature\": 0}`. Sonnet 4.6 still honours temperature. Newer models (Sonnet 5, Opus 4.7 and later, Fable) reject it with a 400 error, so if `MODEL` is ever moved to one of those, this line has to be removed."
  },
